Changes in #285 cause the logic to fail when multiple LSU Read requests are issued. The symptom is observed when hready deasserts to stall the AHB request, in compliance with the AHB-lite specification.

This failing scenario may be reproduced in Calitpra by running the tmp_fpga_repro on this branch:
https://github.com/chipsalliance/caliptra-rtl/tree/cwhitehead-msft-rv-b2b-access-dbg

Specifically, changes to the ahb_htrans signal in https://github.com/chipsalliance/Cores-VeeR-EL2/pull/285/files#diff-49cc6a6800643a1307ae082c5b50091ff340fbb656fa66e6e5abdd8999021448
cause 2 problems:

On back-to-back reads, the htrans signal transitions from 2'b10 (NONSEQ request) to 2'11 (SEQ request) when the state machine enters the STREAM_RD state
This results in the lower 3-bits of buf_addr being masked incorrectly, which forces alignment on the ahb_haddr signal and overrides the buffered request address.



